msgid "Serialization API improvements"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Infinispan 15.0 has been recently released, bringing along a wave of "
"enhancements that\n"
"Quarkus has also embraced. Let's dive into this blog post to spotlight the "
"significant\n"
"updates and improvements for both Infinispan and Quarkus."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Infinispan can handle various serialization formats, but Protobuf stands out "
"as the most\n"
"compatible one, offering full access to all Infinispan Cache features. It's "
"supported through\n"
"the Protostream library. With Protostream 5, you not only get support for "
"Protobuf 3 but also\n"
"a more straightforward and user-friendly API."
msgstr ""

msgid "@Proto"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Using the `@Proto` annotation alone is sufficient to serialize a class, "
"enum, or record with\n"
"Protostream. If you want to be more specific about what needs to be "
"serialized, you can still\n"
"use the `@Protofield` annotation. However, a default schema setup will be "
"automatically handled\n"
"for you with just a single annotation. This feature comes in handy, "
"especially when your\n"
"schema undergoes frequent changes, and you need to refresh data frequently."
msgstr ""

msgid "@ProtoSchema"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The annotation used to define the schema has been renamed to `@ProtoSchema`.\n"
"So now, instead of `@AutoProtoSchemaBuilder`, you would use `@ProtoSchema` "
"for specifying the schema.\n"
"This helps clarify its purpose and usage."
msgstr ""

msgid "Programmatic definition of schemas"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you need to define the schema programmatically, Protostream 5 now offers "
"an API for\n"
"that purpose. This allows you to define the schema dynamically in your code "
"as needed."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Moreover, the `MessageMarshaller` class, which was previously planned for "
"deprecation and removal,\n"
"has been reinstated and can continue to be safely used for implementing "
"custom marshalling."
msgstr ""

msgid "Support for mocks"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Before Quarkus 3.9, because of the Search API, it wasn't possible to mock\n"
"`RemoteCache` beans using `@QuarkusTest` and `@QuarkusMock` due to their "
"`Singleton` scope.\n"
"However, starting from Quarkus 3.9, their scope has been changed to "
"`ApplicationScoped`,\n"
"enabling full mocking for tests."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Additionally, there have been enhancements in the Search API.\n"
"Now, we can directly perform searches using methods exposed in the "
"`RemoteCache` interface."
msgstr ""

msgid "Books cache is injected"
msgstr ""

msgid "Use `query` method directly on the books cache"
msgstr ""

msgid "Retrieve the list as usual"
msgstr ""

msgid "Infinispan Cache extension"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Starting from Quarkus 3.11, the caching annotations in the Infinispan Cache\n"
"extension have been deprecated. Infinispan now offers a new cache extension."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"By swapping out the `quarkus-cache` dependency with `quarkus-infinispan-"
"cache`,\n"
"you can utilize `@CacheResult`, `@CacheInvalidate`, and "
"`@CacheInvalidateAll` annotations\n"
"from the `quarkus-cache` extension, while storing the data in the Infinispan "
"Server."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Read all about it in the https://quarkus.io/guides/cache-infinispan-"
"reference[Infinispan Cache Extension Guide]"
msgstr ""

msgid "Infinispan and Quarkus LangChain4j Integration"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Now, you can use Infinispan as an Embedding Store in the Quarkus LangChain4j "
"extension.\n"
"Infinispan has full text features thanks to a special integration with "
"Hibernate Search.\n"
"Plus, starting from Hibernate Search 7.1, Vector Search is supported. This "
"means you can use the\n"
"Infinispan Server as an Embedding Storage for your LLM applications.\n"
"Read all about it in the https://docs.quarkiverse.io/quarkus-langchain4j/dev/"
"infinispan-store.html[documentation]."
msgstr ""

